<article class="env-lemma" id="0DGC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DGC">Lemma <span data-tag="0DGC">84.5.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. For $K \in D(X_{\acute{e}tale})$ the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  K \longrightarrow R\pi _{X, *}\pi _ X^{-1}K  \]
</div>
  <p> is an isomorphism where $\pi _ X : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits ((\textit{Spaces}/X)_{\acute{e}tale}) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X_{\acute{e}tale})$ is as above. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because both $\pi _ X^{-1}$ and $\pi _{X, *} = i_ X^{-1}$ are exact functors and the composition $\pi _{X, *} \circ \pi _ X^{-1}$ is the identity functor. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>